          "skill": "inferences",
          "passage": "In her 1971 essay \"Why Have There Been No Great Women Artists?\" the art historian Linda Nochlin reframed a question that had usually been answered in biographical terms—by inventorying the careers of individual women painters and asking whether any deserved canonical status. Nochlin instead pointed out that, throughout most of the nineteenth century, European academies barred women from the life-drawing classes that were the principal training ground for ambitious history painters, and that the patronage networks and exhibition juries through which a reputation was built were similarly closed to them. Treating the absence of celebrated women artists as a question about individual genius rather than about institutions, Nochlin's argument therefore implies, ______",
