          "passage": "In her 1962 book *Silent Spring*, marine biologist Rachel Carson assembled a decade of laboratory and field studies on the effects of synthetic pesticides on non-target wildlife. The book did not call for a blanket ban on chemical pest ______ argued, instead, that compounds shown to accumulate in the tissues of birds and other predators should be removed from agricultural use until their long-term ecological effects had been more carefully studied.",
