          "passage": "Aerospace engineer Aprille Ericsson, who designs and analyzes spacecraft instruments at NASA Goddard Space Flight Center, has shown in a series of technical reports that the reaction wheels and articulating mechanisms mounted on a satellite do not act on a perfectly rigid body; their motion couples instead with the bending and twisting of the spacecraft's flexible structure. Even subtle disturbances from these on-board components can therefore carry an instrument's line of sight off target during a long exposure. ______ engineers who try to predict in-orbit pointing performance from a rigid-body model alone routinely overestimate how steadily a large orbiting observatory will hold its angular tolerance.",
