          "passage": "The bioarchaeologist Laurie Reitsema and her colleagues have shown that the carbon and nitrogen ratios locked into the bone collagen of long-buried skeletons preserve a chemical signature of the foods a person ate over the last decade or so of life. Because plants and animals from different parts of a food web carry distinct isotope values, those signatures ______ shifts in the everyday diet of medieval European populations even when no written record of what people ate has survived.",
