          "domain": "craft-and-structure",
          "skill": "words-in-context",
          "passage": "In a long line of laboratory studies, the social psychologist Claude M. Steele found that simply reminding members of a group about a negative stereotype concerning their performance in some domain — say, by mentioning the stereotype on the cover sheet of a difficult test — measurably lowered the scores those participants went on to achieve. Steele argued that the lowered scores did not ______ the test takers' underlying ability in the domain. Instead, the prompt itself loaded working memory with the worry of confirming the stereotype, leaving fewer cognitive resources for the task at hand.",
