              "id": "D",
              "text": "\"Symbiotic merger is not the curiosity it has been treated as; it is, on the evidence we now have, a recurring source of evolutionary novelty in its own right, since the partnership between two formerly independent lineages can deliver, in a single inheritable step, the sort of structural innovation that the gradualist picture of accumulated small advantages within one lineage requires hundreds of generations to assemble.\""
